{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261113T062656Z_dev-05_flat_f49f", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not give a detection significance for the GCE, in σ or as a test statistic. Its template fit finds a nonzero GCE flux in all 80 diffuse-emission models, but the authors say this \"alone does not establish its statistical significance.\" They also say that differences in Δ(−2lnL) between the non-nested diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances. The numbers it does report are goodness-of-fit values for the DM spectral fits to the GCE spectrum, such as χ²_min = 27.50 for 12 degrees of freedom for bb̄. It also reports Δ(−2lnL) of 72.1 to 638.2 for the next five diffuse models relative to Model X. Neither is a detection significance for the excess.", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.1"}]}, "turns": 3, "seconds": 8.962, "tool_calls": 2, "tool_result_chars": 294172, "input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 532, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 129372, "cache_read_input_tokens": 67629, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-13T06:27:05+00:00"}
